    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0262" n="130" xml:id="pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source"> Leahy Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 101 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Commanding General, United States Military Mission
                        in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Deane</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Commanding General, Twelfth Army Group</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bradley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]<anchor n="1" xml:id="d101-f1"/></seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-26">26 June 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For General Bradley and to General Marshall for his eyes only citing <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Shges</hi> [<hi rendition="#italic">sic</hi>] from
                    Deane top sec MX 24797.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . .</p>
                <p>We have already emphasized the importance of General Stoner’s proceeding to
                    Berlin for the signal installations when we asked for authority to increase
                    Parks’ group.</p>
                <p>Upon receipt of your S 93051<anchor n="2" xml:id="d101-f2"/> last night, I again
                    presented the matter to General Antonov and Harriman presented it to
                        Vyshinski.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d101-f3"/> I shall see General Antonov or
                    his representatives today and press the matter further.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
